@@@!atrep-exo
@=kolophon=>docbook

@@/ DocBook export of a colophon, as children of an info: the
@@/ publisher's name, the place as an address holding a city,
@@/ the date as pubdate, any other field a bibliomisc whose role
@@/ is the field name. All four stand directly in an info; the
@@/ enclosing info is written by the host exo.

@%
& &amp;
< &lt;
> &gt;
" &quot;
%@

@-> *paragraph
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> :(officina)
<publishername>@(grammata)</publishername>
>-@

@-> :(locus)
<address><city>@(grammata)</city></address>
>-@

@-> :(datum)
<pubdate>@(grammata)</pubdate>
>-@

@-> :
<bibliomisc role="@(lemma)">@(grammata)</bibliomisc>
>-@
